<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Islamic Movement of Uzbekistan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1998">1998</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Islamic Movement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a> was a militant Islamist group founded in 1998 by Tahir Yuldashev and Juma Namangani with the aim of overthrowing President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam-karimov">Islam Karimov</a>. Based in Tajikistan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, it made armed incursions into Kyrgyzstan and Uzbekistan in 1999 and 2000. It fought alongside the Taliban after 2001, lost Namangani, and later moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> before declaring allegiance to the Islamic State in 2015.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/islamic-movement-of-uzbekistan.jpg" alt="Islamic Movement of Uzbekistan" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Jihad.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
